messages.content:
Below is a minimal, ready-to-run example for Textual 0.8.x that matches what you described:

- Header and Footer
- A block of static text under the header
- A main container with a larger output area (TextLog) and a smaller input area below it (TextArea + Send button)
- The smaller input area is set to ~11 lines high

Save as app.py and run python app.py.

from textual.app import App, ComposeResult
from textual.containers import Container, Vertical
from textual.widgets import Header, Footer, Static, Button, TextArea, TextLog

class MessagePageApp(App):
    CSS = """
    Screen {
        padding: 1;
        spacing: 1;
    }

    #intro {
        padding: 1;
    }

    #panel {
        border: tall $surface;
        padding: 0;
        height: 1fr; /* let panel take available space */
        display: vertical;
    }

    #output {
        border: round $accent;
        height: 1fr;     /* fill remaining space above input */
        padding: 1;
        overflow: auto;
    }

    #input-area {
        border: heavy $accent;
        height: 11;      /* ~11 lines high for the small input area */
        padding: 1;
        layout: horizontal;
        gap: 1;
    }

    TextArea {
        width: 1fr;      /* take most of the input-area width */
    }

    Button#send {
        width: 12;
    }
    """

    def compose(self) -> ComposeResult:
        yield Header()
        yield Static("This is a simple page. Type a message in the box below and press Send to print it into the larger area.", id="intro")

        with Container(id="panel"):
            yield TextLog(id="output")                 # large output area
            with Container(id="input-area"):           # smaller input area underneath
                yield TextArea(id="input", placeholder="Type your message here (multi-line allowed)...")
                yield Button("Send", id="send", variant="primary")

        yield Footer()

    def on_button_pressed(self, event: Button.Pressed) -> None:
        if event.button.id == "send":
            textarea = self.query_one("#input", TextArea)
            text = textarea.value or ""
            text = text.rstrip("\n")
            if text.strip():
                output = self.query_one("#output", TextLog)
                # Write the whole block (preserves multiple lines)
                for line in text.splitlines():
                    output.write(line)
                output.write("")  # add a blank line for spacing
                textarea.clear()

if __name__ == "__main__":
    MessagePageApp().run()

Notes and small tweaks
- If your installed Textual version does not provide TextArea (rare in older alphas), replace TextArea with a regular Input and accept single-line messages, or use a third-party multiline widget. If you need that fallback example, tell me and I’ll provide it.
- You can also submit with a keybinding (Ctrl+Enter) by adding a key handler on the TextArea if you prefer not to click Send.
- Adjust the CSS height of #input-area to within 9–11 if you want it slightly smaller or larger.
